    "result_text": "Done. `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response is serialized from the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto`, mapped from `Owner` via MapStruct. To add `initials` with minimal structural impact, I made two small, cohesive changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared a new read-only `initials` property on the `Owner` schema (mirroring the existing `displayName` field), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and it appears in the JSON.\n\n2. **`Person.java`** \u2014 added a single `getInitials()` method (CC 1) to the small `Person` class, which already owns `firstName`/`lastName`. MapStruct auto-maps it by name, so **no change to the large `Owner` class and no change to `OwnerMapper`** were needed.\n\n```java\npublic String getInitials() {\n    return Character.toUpperCase(this.firstName.charAt(0)) + \".\"\n        + Character.toUpperCase(this.lastName.charAt(0)) + \".\";\n}\n```\n\n`firstName`/`lastName` are `@NotEmpty`, so `charAt(0)` is safe. `john`/`smith` \u2192 `J.S.` as the test expects.\n\nPlacing the method on `Person` (WMC_other \u2248 6 accessors) rather than `Owner` (much larger WMC_other), and letting name-based automapping avoid editing the mapper, keeps the changed-function cost low.",
